<p><code>pop-config</code> wraps configuration data in an object that reads like an array, an object or a dot path,
loads from five file formats, and refuses writes unless you ask for them. <code>Pop\Application</code> takes one
directly, so the config an application boots with can be a <code>Config</code> instance rather than a bare array.</p>
